    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="session-api" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Session API</h2>
    <p>
      The typed session API in <code>server/httpapi/session.ts</code> is the compact source for the
      main SDK contract. The classic <code>routes/session.ts</code> file exposes the same domain plus
      richer event-stream and compatibility routes.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/session</code></td><td>List sessions, filtered by directory, roots, start timestamp, search, and limit.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/session</code></td><td>Create a session with optional parent, title, permission rules, skills, GitHub metadata, and workspace id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/session/status</code></td><td>Return the current session status map.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GET/PATCH/DELETE</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID</code></td><td>Read, update title/archive time, or remove a session.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID/fork</code></td><td>Fork from a session, optionally at a message id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID/abort</code></td><td>Cancel prompt execution, owned delegation jobs, and monitors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID/revert</code></td><td>Revert the diff associated with a message or part.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID/unrevert</code></td><td>Undo the previous revert.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID/message</code></td><td>List messages, optionally limited.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GET/PATCH/DELETE</td><td><code>/session/:sessionID/message/:messageID</code></td><td>Read or remove a message; patch/remove individual parts through the nested part route.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="mobile-api" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Mobile API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>routes/mobile.ts</code> is intentionally larger than the base API because it exposes
      a complete phone workflow: bootstrap, pairing tokens, account state, sessions, git review,
      GitHub repo import, workspace/container execution, terminal tabs, settings, MCP, plugins,
      routines, approvals, and streaming.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Route area</th><th>Examples</th><th>Used by</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Pairing and bootstrap</td><td><code>/mobile/auth/token</code>, <code>/mobile/bootstrap</code></td><td>Connect screen and host smoke tests.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sessions</td><td><code>/mobile/sessions</code>, stream endpoints, prompt endpoints</td><td>Sessions tab and chat screen.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Permissions/questions</td><td>Approval and question reply endpoints</td><td>Composer approval bars and pending prompts.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Git and files</td><td>Status, diff, commit, file tree, editor endpoints</td><td>Git review and editor screens.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Repos and GitHub</td><td>Repo search/import/session launch endpoints</td><td>Repos tab and GitHub-backed workspaces.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Terminal</td><td>PTY create/list/input/resize/close endpoints</td><td>Terminal tab.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Routines</td><td>Routine CRUD, run, pause, resume, API trigger endpoints</td><td>Routines tab.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="note" title="Prefer narrow mobile smokes">
      <p>
        <code>POST /mobile/auth/token</code> is a better first host smoke than
        <code>/mobile/bootstrap</code> because bootstrap touches more subsystems, including project
        detection, GitHub, Expo, container runtime, and config.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="httpapi" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Effect HttpApi bridge</h2>
    <p>
      The typed API groups use <code>effect/unstable/httpapi</code>. They are mounted through
      <code>HttpApiBridge</code> only when <code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_HTTPAPI</code> is truthy and
      the bridge says a request path and method are supported.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Source</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Session</td><td><code>httpapi/session.ts</code></td><td>Normalizes undefined fields by JSON round trip before returning unknown-shaped session payloads.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>File</td><td><code>httpapi/file.ts</code></td><td>Find text, find file, symbol search, list, read, write, status.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MCP</td><td><code>httpapi/mcp.ts</code></td><td>Status, add, OAuth start/callback/authenticate, auth removal, connect/disconnect, toggle.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Provider</td><td><code>httpapi/provider.ts</code></td><td>Provider list, auth methods, API token write, auth removal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Config</td><td><code>httpapi/config.ts</code></td><td>Read and update config plus provider summary.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Workspace</td><td><code>httpapi/workspace.ts</code></td><td>Adaptors, create/list/remove/restore, session restore, warp.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Brain</td><td><code>httpapi/brain.ts</code></td><td>Brain model picker and scheduler state, periodic re-evaluation triggers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ChatBot</td><td><code>httpapi/chatbot.ts</code></td><td>Bot config CRUD, restart, and webhook delivery state.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sync</td><td><code>httpapi/sync.ts</code></td><td>Hub push, snapshot, config, and stats endpoints. See <a href="/docs/sync">Sync</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pty</td><td><code>httpapi/pty.ts</code></td><td>PTY lifecycle: create, list, input, resize, close, websocket upgrade.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Doctor</td><td><code>httpapi/doctor.ts</code></td><td>Health diagnostics used by the <code>nikcli doctor</code> command and the web app.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Analytics</td><td><code>httpapi/analytics.ts</code></td><td>Typed analytics summaries and drilldowns.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Loop</td><td><code>httpapi/loop.ts</code></td><td>Typed CRUD and run / pause / resume / schedule for <a href="/docs/loops">Loops</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Top-level</td><td><code>httpapi/top-level.ts</code></td><td>Path, VCS, command, agent, skill, LSP, formatter, dispose.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="streaming" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Events and streaming</h2>
    <p>
      The server uses two event styles. Hono routes stream server-sent events where a client needs
      a long-lived feed, while many TUI, permission, MCP, and session state changes also publish
      internal <code>BusEvent</code> events.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>streamSSE</code> is imported in the server and mobile route layers for live feeds.</li>
      <li><code>TuiRoutes</code> publish <code>TuiEvent.CommandExecute</code> so external clients can open dialogs or run commands in the active TUI.</li>
      <li>Permission and question routes publish request/reply events through their services.</li>
      <li>MCP publishes <code>mcp.tools.changed</code> when a connected server sends a tool-list notification.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="openapi" class="doc-section">
    <h2>OpenAPI docs</h2>
    <p>
      <code>GET /doc</code> uses <code>openAPIRouteHandler</code> from <code>hono-openapi</code>
      against the Hono app. Classic route files use <code>describeRoute</code>, validators, and
      resolvers to contribute route metadata.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
curl http://127.0.0.1:4096/doc
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="SDK regeneration">
      <p>
        Docs-only edits do not require SDK regeneration. If a server endpoint contract changes in
        <code>packages/nikcli/src/server/server.ts</code> or typed HttpApi route files, regenerate
        the JavaScript SDK with <code>./packages/sdk/js/script/build.ts</code>.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-modes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Failure modes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Check</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>401 on every request</td><td>Missing bearer token, Basic Auth password mismatch, or Tailscale identity header absent.</td><td>Check auth headers and <code>NIKCLI_SERVER_PASSWORD</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Workspace not found</td><td><code>x-nikcli-workspace</code> points at a workspace with no target.</td><td>Call workspace list or remove stale workspace id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Route handled by old implementation</td><td><code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_HTTPAPI</code> is unset or bridge does not support that method/path.</td><td>Inspect <code>HttpApiBridge.supports</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CORS preflight fails</td><td>Origin is not local, app, Tailscale, <code>nikcli.store</code>, or whitelisted.</td><td>Set <code>NIKCLI_SERVER_CORS_ORIGINS</code> for custom origins.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mobile bootstrap is slow</td><td>Bootstrap hits project, GitHub, Expo, container, provider, and config checks.</td><td>Smoke <code>/mobile/auth/token</code> first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Unknown error JSON</td><td>Error did not match known domain classes.</td><td>Use <code>--print-logs</code> and inspect <code>Global.Path.log</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

